user_prompt:
Hi Grace,

Evaluate the cover letter draft for accuracy only.

Verify every factual claim against {$FIRST_NAME}'s source materials (base resume, backstory, strengths, priorities, LinkedIn, bio), the final resume, and the JD. Pay particular attention to attribution: a real metric attached to the wrong company or the wrong project is a fabrication. For each issue, quote the source that supports or contradicts the claim and name the document.

Style, tone, and structure are not your scope.

Output one JSON object exactly:
{
  "agent_performance": {"status": "success | failure", "failure_note": ""},
  "agent_payload": {
    "verdict": "clean | issues_found",
    "issues": [{"severity": "high | medium | low", "claim": "", "source_check": {"document": "", "quote": "", "supports": false}, "required_fix": ""}]
  }
}

Hi Judith,

Grace's fact-check on your letter is below. Produce the final letter.

Same discipline as the resume pass: for each issue, FIX (correct to what the source supports) or DEFEND (quote the candidate-context line Grace missed). Keep the THESIS, the STORY, and the QUESTION intact unless an issue makes them untrue; accuracy repairs change facts, not voice. Stay under 300 words. The WRITING INSTRUCTIONS apply; scan for banned characters before you output.

Output one JSON object exactly:
{
  "agent_performance": {"status": "success | failure", "failure_note": ""},
  "agent_payload": {
    "re_line": "", "body": "", "signature": "{$FIRST_NAME} {$LAST_NAME}",
    "dispositions": [{"claim": "", "action": "fixed | defended", "note": ""}]
  }
}

